---
description: Commit and push validated Deliobot deliveries to main
alwaysApply: true
---

- Every completed delivery includes committing and pushing its intended changes to `origin/main`.
- Fetch main first, integrate concurrent changes and resolve conflicts without discarding others' work.
- Run the checks appropriate to the final merged changes before pushing.
- Never force-push main or bypass required checks and protections.
- Keep secrets, generated build artifacts and temporary verification data out of Git.
- Verify the remote main commit after the push. Report source publication and deployment separately.
- If authentication, permissions or branch protection prevents the push, report the exact remaining blocker; do not claim it succeeded.
